From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:35:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Use system-memory sink for live video

Proton Experimental's working GStreamer path does not connect the live HLS
video topology to the D3D-aware frame sink. The winedmo path does, but native
AVPro consumers can fail to observe those DXGI-backed frames even though
TransferVideoFrame successfully copies changing pixels into their texture.

Keep the frame sink in system memory for media without a finite duration and
let Media Engine's normal renderer upload and draw those samples. This mirrors
the working topology without changing finite media or disabling the engine's
D3D device manager for the application-owned destination texture.
---
 dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1409,7 +1409,11 @@ static HRESULT media_engine_create_video_renderer(struct media_engine *engine, I
     IMFMediaType_SetGUID(media_type, &MF_MT_MAJOR_TYPE, &MFMediaType_Video);
     IMFMediaType_SetGUID(media_type, &MF_MT_SUBTYPE, &subtype);
 
-    hr = create_video_frame_sink(media_type, (IUnknown *)engine->device_manager, &engine->sink_events, &engine->presentation.frame_sink);
+    if (isinf(engine->duration))
+        WARN("Using a system-memory video sink for live media.\n");
+    hr = create_video_frame_sink(media_type,
+            isinf(engine->duration) ? NULL : (IUnknown *)engine->device_manager,
+            &engine->sink_events, &engine->presentation.frame_sink);
     IMFMediaType_Release(media_type);
     if (FAILED(hr))
         return hr;
@@ -3502,7 +3506,8 @@ static HRESULT media_engine_transfer_d3d11(struct media_engine *engine, ID3D11Te
     hr = get_d3d11_resource_from_sample(sample, &src_texture, &subresource);
     if (FAILED(hr))
     {
-        hr = media_engine_transfer_d3d11_memory(engine, sample, dst_texture, src_rect, dst_rect);
+        if (!isinf(engine->duration))
+            hr = media_engine_transfer_d3d11_memory(engine, sample, dst_texture, src_rect, dst_rect);
         IMFSample_Release(sample);
         return hr;
     }
